    # Presentations

    ## [SCEMENT](https://doi.org/10.1093/bioinformatics/btaf057)
    SCEMENT is a software implementing our scalable and memory efficient 
    integration method of large-scale single cell RNA-sequencing data. 
    SCEMENT ias published in the paper
    [10.1093/bioinformatics/btaf057](https://doi.org/10.1093/bioinformatics/btaf057).
    My presentation in AWSOM'25 is [here in pdf version](/assets/docs/scement.pdf)
    
    ## [Airavata Cerebrum](https://doi.org/10.1093/bioinformatics/btaf057)
    Airava Cerebrum is wn Integrated Computational Neuroscience 
    Framework, whose goal is to build computational neuroscience models
    that can be constructed using large single-cell datasets from Brain Atlases.
    Python source is available at 
    [github](https://github.com/apache/airavata‑cerebrum).
    My presentation in Cybershuttle workshop'25 is 
    [here](/assets/docs/cerebrum-presentation.pdf).
    The poster I presented at SfN Neuroscience conference is 
    [here](/assets/docs/cerebrum-poster.pdf).

    ## [Ph.d Thesis and Defense](https://bitbucket.org/srirampc/phd-thesis/)
    My Ph.d. thesis is on the topic of 
    __Parallel Algorithmic Techniques for Large-Scale Problems in Computational Biology__.
    Slides of my defense  are available 
    [here](https://bitbucket.org/srirampc/phd-thesis/src/master/defense/defense.pdf).
    LaTeX source of my thesis, defence and synopis are in the bitbucker repository
    [here](https://bitbucket.org/srirampc/phd-thesis/)
